localsend-cli: no `AtomicU64` on targets without 64-bit atomics (32-bit PowerPC)

mrustc on powerpc-apple-darwin, building the `localsend` core crate for localsend-cli 1.18.2:

    packages/core/src/discovery/mod.rs:17:5-58 error:0: Unable to resolve `use` target ::"std"::sync::atomic::AtomicU64

32-bit PowerPC, MIPS and older ARM have no 64-bit atomics, so `std::sync::atomic::AtomicU64`
does not exist there (`cfg(target_has_atomic = "64")` is unset). Two kinds of use in the tree:

- packages/core `DiscoveryState::confirmations`: a count of confirmations that
  `discover_staged` compares with an earlier value of itself to see whether any arrived.
  `AtomicUsize` is enough (identical on 64-bit targets).
- cli `send_task` / `app::receive` / `app::sending` progress counters: cumulative bytes,
  read by `app::status` and `done_bytes`. A narrower atomic would truncate transfers over
  4 GiB, so a new `cli/src/atomic64.rs` keeps them `u64`: `std`'s `AtomicU64` where the
  target has 64-bit atomics, else a `Mutex<u64>` with the same `new`/`load`/`store`
  surface (the only operations used). Other targets compile exactly the code they did.

packages/core/tests/v2_server.rs and v2_tls_pinning.rs use `AtomicU64` too; they are not
built by the port and are left alone. `server` and `packages/localsend_isolates/rust` have none.

